course: dictionary
lesson: 6739
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to another alphabet. Omega is the last letter of the Greek alphabet, written Ω in capitals or ω in small letters. Its first letter is alpha, so the two together are a pair that covers the start and the finish.
explain: «The alpha and the omega» means the beginning and the end. In the Bible's Book of Revelation, God says «I am the Alpha and the Omega», which means he is the beginning and the end of everything.
explain: Omega has other meanings too. Omega-3 is a healthy fat in oily fish, and Ω is the science symbol for ohms, a unit of electrical resistance. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «Cod-liver oil contains omega-3 fats and vitamins A and D» tells you omega-3 is a fat, not a letter, because it sits with fats and vitamins.
fact: Omega is the last letter of the Greek alphabet.
fact: It is written Ω in capitals and ω in small letters.
fact: «The alpha and the omega» means the beginning and the end.
fact: Omega-3 is a kind of healthy fat found in oily fish.
fact: Ω is the symbol for ohms, the unit of electrical resistance.
exercise: What is omega? | *The last letter of the Greek alphabet | A loud noise made by a bell | The first letter of the English alphabet | A kind of oily fish
exercise: «The alpha and the omega» means what? | *The beginning and the end | The middle of a race | A pair of shoes | Two kinds of fish
exercise: «Cod-liver oil contains omega-3 fats and vitamins A and D.» What kind of thing is omega-3 here? | *A healthy fat | A Greek letter | A unit of electricity | A type of fish
test: Which symbol is the capital letter omega? | Π | Σ | *Ω | Ψ
test: In science, what does the symbol Ω stand for? | A kind of vitamin | The end of a book | *Ohms, the unit of electrical resistance | Oil taken from fish
exam: Which sentence uses omega to mean the beginning and the end? | The ohm is shown by the symbol Ω on the plug | Mum buys omega-3 at the shop on Friday | I finished the race at the omega line | *God says, «I am the Alpha and the Omega»
